{"id":"21883c1f18074c7bacb2b34de8304154","owner":"esri_landscape2","created":1588813926000,"modified":1664819786000,"guid":null,"name":"USA_Historic_Sites_PADUS","title":"USA Historic Sites","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service","View Service"],"description":"Historic sites include areas where significant historical events of cultural interest occurred. These range from National Historic Parks, Sites, Trails, and Preserves to state, local, and areas held in trust.<div><br /><\/div><div><div><font size='4'>Dataset Summary<\/font><\/div><div><br /><\/div><div><b>Phenomenon Mapped<\/b>: Historic Sites from the Protected Areas Database of the United States version 3.0<\/div><div><b>Coordinate System<\/b>: Web Mercator Auxiliary Sphere<\/div><div><b>Extent<\/b>: 50 United States and Guam<\/div><div><b>Visible Scale<\/b>: Visible at all scales<\/div><div><b>Source<\/b>: USGS National Gap Analysis Program PAD-US version 3.0<\/div><div><b>Publication Date<\/b>: July 2022<\/div><div><br /><\/div><div><font size='4'>What can you do with this layer?<\/font><\/div><div><br /><\/div><div>This layer can be used to create maps and to visualize the underlying data across the ArcGIS platform. It can also be used as an analytic input in ArcGIS Online.<\/div><div><br /><\/div><div>The data can be exported to a file geodatabase, a shape file or other format and downloaded using the Export Data button on the top right of the description page.<\/div><\/div>","tags":["PADUS","PAD-US","landscape","hosted","esri_environment","landcover","esri_landscape","environment","historic","PADUS 3.0"],"snippet":"Historic Sites from the Protected Areas Database of the United States version 3.0.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail1588815305303.jpeg","documentation":null,"extent":[[-159.66594245932342,13.377121685749774],[145.73173996300977,61.800898006197485]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"102100","